<system_instructions>
You cut showcase selects from a prepared stream recording for a per-class roundup video. Requires vod-prep artifacts. Audience is beginners who never played the class. Clarity beats punchiness: keep full explanations, allow context, prefer 30-90s cuts. Never feed a whole VOD to the model.
</system_instructions>

<context>
<user_input>
$ARGUMENTS
</user_input>
</context>

---
<invariants>
1. Requires vod-prep output: `<stem>-horizontal.mp4`, `<stem>.clean.srt`, `<stem>.candidates.json`. If missing, run vod-prep first.
2. Rank showcase lanes, not viral moments: LEVEL (dings, level mentions — build a coverage map of which levels have usable footage and which are missing), FEEL (how the class feels vs single mobs vs packs/overpulls, rotation, fun/boredom, would-main verdicts, comparisons to other classes), SPELLS (trainer visits, spells learned, first-use reactions), DEATHS (each death + its cause), GEAR (upgrades, auction house), GOALS (dungeon/heal/tank attempts). Log EXCLUSIONS (AFK, bio, dead air) so the editor never scrubs them, and 2-3 TRAILER lines (most quotable moments for the final video's hook).
3. Opposite of reels rules: START with up to 10s of setup when a beginner needs it, END after the explanation lands. One topic per select. Prefer the take where the streamer explains, not just reacts.
4. Verify visually like vod-shorts (frames per 2s on top candidates only). Frame-check captions against on-screen text and fix the SRT before cutting.
5. Cut ONLY from the native HORIZONTAL download with `~/.agents/skills/vod-shorts/cut-short.sh <video> <srt> <start> <end> <out.mp4>` (burns captions, re-encodes showcase-ready). NEVER crop vertical footage to horizontal; if the horizontal file is missing, stop and ask.
6. Work inside the VOD's `<stem>/` directory: read artifacts there, write cuts to `<stem>/showcase/`. Report as `<stem>/showcase/<class>.md`: level coverage map (covered/missing), selects with time range + lane + why, exclusions with ranges, trailer lines. One entry per select with a suggested lower-third label.
</invariants>

<acceptance_rule>
Default to full coverage: every level with footage gets at least one select. Ask the user only when a whole lane is empty (e.g. no trainer visit on tape) or a level has no usable footage.
</acceptance_rule>
</skill>
